{title: My Heart Exults in the Lord}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 2:1–8}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
My heart exults in the Lord
My strength is lifted up in the Lord
[Abmaj7]There is none holy like the Lord
There is [Bb]none besides [Cm]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The Lord brings low and he lifts up
He raises the poor from the dust
He lifts the needy from the ash heap
To [Bb]sit with [Cm]princes
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The bows of the mighty are broken
The feeble are clothed with strength
The barren has borne seven
The [Bb]Lord kills and brings to [Cm]life
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Bb] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] |
